From: mwlaboratories <info@mwlabs.be>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: imx371, imx376: allow analogue gain up to 16x

Both drivers cap the analogue gain code at 480. These sensors take
1024 / (1024 - code), so 480 is only about 1.9x and the cameras stay
dark in low light. The OnePlus OxygenOS sensor library clamps the code
at 960, which is 16x; the OnePlus 6T postmarketOS camera stack
(github.com/lolren/oneplus6t-pmos-fixes) raises the limit the same way.

Status: hypothesis until tested on the OnePlus 6.
---
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx371.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx371.c
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@
 
 /* Analog gain control */
 #define IMX371_ANA_GAIN_MIN		0
-#define IMX371_ANA_GAIN_MAX		480
+#define IMX371_ANA_GAIN_MAX		960
 #define IMX371_ANA_GAIN_STEP		1
 #define IMX371_ANA_GAIN_DEFAULT		0x0
 
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx376.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx376.c
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@
 
 /* Analog gain control */
 #define IMX376_ANA_GAIN_MIN		0
-#define IMX376_ANA_GAIN_MAX		480
+#define IMX376_ANA_GAIN_MAX		960
 #define IMX376_ANA_GAIN_STEP		1
 #define IMX376_ANA_GAIN_DEFAULT		0x0
 
